KZ3 patch 1120 (SPU pass 103): the part of upstream ps3recomp PR #434 our set lacks (MIT; author: tekulvw, https://github.com/sp00nznet/ps3recomp/pull/434). POSIX hosts use _setjmp/_longjmp for the SPU halt, stack-reset, resume
and IRQ jumps (no sigprocmask per jump): SPU_SETJMP (patch 1099's macro, spu_context.h) gains the POSIX branch and
SPU_LONGJMP is new; Windows keeps patch 1099's frameless _setjmp(buf, NULL) and plain longjmp (the PR's own
definition in spu_channels.c would have redefined SPU_SETJMP as plain setjmp on Windows and undone 1099). The rest of
the PR is already in our set in KZ3's form: t_recent (one TLS object in the PR) is the per-context step ring of
patches 1068/1086, spu_task_launch_check's fast path is patch 1039's inline form, spu_depth_guard's shared ring was
removed by 1086, and spu_check_stack_reset is reached only when the registry is non-empty (1039 inline test, 1017
order). Windows objects of spu_channels.c and spu_drain.c are instruction-identical with and without this patch.
Notes the RE notes Pass 103.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
index 5cd19e48..331d5d15 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@ int (*g_kz3_spurs_kpoll)(uint32_t, uint32_t, uint32_t, uint32_t*) = 0;
 void spu_task_cutoff_exit(spu_context* ctx)
 {
     g_spu_trampoline_fn = 0;
-    if (s_spu_halt_armed) { s_spu_halt_armed = 0; longjmp(s_spu_halt_env, 1); }
+    if (s_spu_halt_armed) { s_spu_halt_armed = 0; SPU_LONGJMP(s_spu_halt_env, 1); }
     fprintf(stderr, "[ts-join] cut-off task outside the execution driver at 0x%05X: resumes\n", ctx->pc);
 }
 
diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_context.h b/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
index 633e9c5f..7e17fa26 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
@@ -43,10 +43,20 @@
  * pass 73: the K2 audio policy module stalled at its first halt longjmp). The SPU runtime's halt and stack-reset
  * jumps run no unwind handlers, so they use the frameless form (_setjmp(buf, NULL): longjmp only restores the
  * saved registers). */
+/* Upstream PR #434 (KZ3 patch 1120): setjmp/longjmp also save and restore the signal mask on POSIX: one
+ * sigprocmask system call per halt, stack reset or task resume. These frames never cross a signal handler, so the
+ * mask is the same at both ends: POSIX hosts use _setjmp/_longjmp. Windows keeps the forms above (patch 1099). */
 #if SPU_SYSV_ABI && defined(_WIN64) && defined(__MINGW64__)
 #  define SPU_SETJMP(b) _setjmp((b), NULL)
-#else
+#elif defined(_WIN32)
 #  define SPU_SETJMP(b) setjmp(b)
+#else
+#  define SPU_SETJMP(b) _setjmp(b)
+#endif
+#if defined(_WIN32)
+#  define SPU_LONGJMP(b, v) longjmp((b), (v))
+#else
+#  define SPU_LONGJMP(b, v) _longjmp((b), (v))
 #endif
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
